{"styles":[{"sc":"#ff2600","so":1,"w":2,"ol":true,"fc":"#fffb00","fo":0.502}],"cards":["<div style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#222222;max-width:238px;\"><div style=\"background:#0e7d46;height:6px;border-radius:3px 3px 0 0;\"></div><div style=\"font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#0e7d46;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;padding:7px 0 0;\">COUNTY BOUNDARY</div><div style=\"font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#0e7d46;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;padding:0 0 2px;\">VIRGINIA</div><div style=\"font-size:16px;font-weight:800;padding:2px 0 6px;\">Virginia Beach City County</div><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px;\"><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Population</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">453,737 (2025 est.)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">County Seat</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">Virginia Beach</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Land Area</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">245 sq mi</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Density</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">1,852 / sq mi</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Median Household Income</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">$90,685</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Median Home Value</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">$366,300</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#333333;padding:8px 0 2px;border-top:1px solid #eef2f1;margin-top:7px;\">Virginia Beach is an independent city with its own zoning, schools and tax base, the most populous locality in Virginia, built on the military presence at Naval Air Station Oceana and Joint Expeditionary Base Little Creek-Fort Story, resort tourism, and a Town Center office core that functions as the city's CBD. Two hard constraints define the deal set, the AICUZ noise and accident-potential zones around Oceana that restrict use and density across a large share of the city, and the Green Line that holds back urban services in the southern agricultural half, while the transatlantic cable landings have opened a technology and data-center niche on the north end.</div><div style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888888;padding-top:6px;\">Source: U.S. Census Bureau · Data verified: September 24, 2026</div></div>"],"feats":[["Virginia Beach City",0,[[36.83385,-76.22776],[36.83287,-76.22806],[36.83198,-76.22776],[36.83184,-76.22776],[36.82927,-76.22683],[36.82654,-76.22581],[36.82485,-76.22515],[36.82448,-76.22492],[36.82079,-76.22359],[36.81981,-76.22316],[36.81854,-76.22271],[36.81516,-76.22137],[36.81417,-76.2206],[36.81285,-76.22016],[36.81225,-76.21986],[36.81005,-76.21896],[36.80704,-76.21796],[36.80548,-76.21723],[36.80415,-76.21665],[36.80414,-76.21671],[36.80351,-76.21647],[36.80354,-76.21635],[36.80244,-76.21606],[36.79656,-76.2138],[36.79605,-76.21366],[36.79416,-76.21288],[36.76966,-76.20367],[36.76475,-76.18855],[36.7641,-76.18716],[36.76375,-76.18653],[36.7634,-76.18364],[36.76309,-76.18179],[36.76284,-76.18086],[36.76236,-76.17753],[36.76109,-76.1698],[36.75956,-76.15931],[36.75815,-76.15176],[36.75715,-76.14336],[36.73495,-76.11886],[36.71675,-76.09846],[36.71605,-76.09755],[36.71478,-76.09318],[36.71366,-76.08893],[36.71345,-76.08795],[36.71245,-76.08215],[36.71145,-76.08165],[36.70574,-76.08035],[36.69925,-76.07515],[36.69655,-76.07275],[36.69441,-76.07014],[36.69258,-76.068],[36.69211,-76.06781],[36.68555,-76.06555],[36.67745,-76.06915],[36.67845,-76.07395],[36.67725,-76.07685],[36.67865,-76.07965],[36.67705,-76.08395],[36.67585,-76.08615],[36.67505,-76.09245],[36.67495,-76.09375],[36.67485,-76.09395],[36.67465,-76.09535],[36.67335,-76.09985],[36.67045,-76.10066],[36.66995